From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fix TX scheduler queue mask loop upper bound

Backport of Wayen Yan's net patch (v3), rebased 2026-06-20 onto master's
airoha_qdma_deref() refactor (set_chan_tx_sched now derefs qdma into a
local instead of using dev->qdma).

airoha_qdma_set_chan_tx_sched() looped over AIROHA_NUM_TX_RING (32) while
clearing TXQ_DISABLE_CHAN_QUEUE_MASK(channel, i) = BIT(i + (channel&3)*8),
shifting past bit 31 of a 32-bit register. There are only
AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES (8) queues per channel; bound the loop there.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2801,7 +2801,7 @@
 	int i;
 
 	qdma = airoha_qdma_deref(dev);
-	for (i = 0; i < AIROHA_NUM_TX_RING; i++)
+	for (i = 0; i < AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES; i++)
 		airoha_qdma_clear(qdma, REG_QUEUE_CLOSE_CFG(channel),
 				  TXQ_DISABLE_CHAN_QUEUE_MASK(channel, i));
 
